{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"crumbly-amphibole-smelts","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, authorized at full scope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\nThis is deliverable 1 + the net-mechanism half of deliverable 3 (its red proof).\n\n## The gap\n\n`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py` is a shrink-only ratchet over\n`.github/mechanism-baseline.json`. It censuses seven mechanism kinds — `lock`, `env_var`,\n`config_key`, `feature_flag`, `ci_gate`, `autouse_fixture`, `test_helper` — and fails the\nbuild on any `new>0`. A new mechanism is admitted by an in-tree marker\n`# mechanism-ok: <kind> <name> — <reason or ticket id>` at the definition site.\n\nThe ratchet therefore asks \"is this mechanism justified?\" and never asks \"is the system\nnet-simpler afterward?\". A plan may add a mechanism, write a one-line reason, and pass —\nwith nothing retired. The ratchet's own docstring records why this matters: 56% of sampled\nfixes added a mechanism against 30% that were pure logic fixes.\n\nPlan review does not close the gap either. `A1` (over-engineering, NIH,\nconfig-surface proliferation) is the only complexity criterion and it is ADVISORY, so it\ncannot block.\n\n## The change\n\nA new BLOCKING plan-review criterion. A plan whose edit set adds a mechanism of a kind the\nratchet counts must either name the mechanism it retires, or carry an explicit\njustification for why no retirement is possible. Absent both, the criterion blocks.\n\nThe criterion reasons about the PLAN, not the tree — it runs at claim time, before any\ncode exists. It is therefore a judgement about what the plan says it will add, cross-read\nagainst what it says it will remove.\n\n## Portability\n\nPer the blocking `project.portability` criterion, a check whose only trigger is a specific\nCI system is not portable. This criterion runs inside plan review, which is an\noperation-linked in-process path with no CI dependency, so it satisfies portability by\nconstruction. The plan must state that explicitly rather than leave it inferred.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nrebar must support a wide variety of providers and models. The rubric must not assume a\nsingle vendor's model, must not depend on vendor-specific tool-calling syntax, and must be\nexpressed in the same prompt form every other packaged criterion uses.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A new criterion id exists with both a rubric prompt and a routing entry, and its\n      routing posture is blocking. Verified by a test asserting the registry reports the\n      criterion as blocking.\n- [ ] The registry coverage check passes with the new criterion present — every canonical\n      criterion has a prompt and a routing entry. Verified by the existing coverage test.\n- [ ] RED PROOF: a plan that adds a mechanism, names no retired mechanism, and carries no\n      justification produces a BLOCK from this criterion. Verified against a named ticket\n      from the breaking pass that landed a mechanism and should have been caught.\n- [ ] A plan that adds a mechanism AND names the mechanism it retires produces no finding\n      from this criterion. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] A plan that adds no mechanism produces no finding from this criterion — the\n      criterion does not fire on unrelated plans. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` is regenerated and the guide-parity check\n      passes. Verified by the existing guide-parity test.\n- [ ] `rebar explain <new-criterion-id>` returns the criterion's section. Verified by a\n      test.\n- [ ] The criterion fires with no CI provider present. Verified by a test that exercises\n      it with no CI environment configured.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Plan grounding\n\nExact file:line citations for the prompt directory, the routing file and its posture\nfield, the coverage check, the guide regeneration command, and the vocabulary allowlist\nare being measured against `origin/main` and will be written into this description before\nplan review is requested. This ticket is NOT ready for review until that is done.","id":"fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7","parent_id":"77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Add a blocking net-mechanism plan-review criterion: adding a mechanism must name what it retires"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793647918651154327,"uuid":"a37c4476-ee75-4e0d-bde7-c36f3e7b3f91"}